Honoured sir,

Arrangements for the wine shipment from Gascony are as follows: carts at dawn=
, the household to follow, and the heavy plate to go by water.

I trust this note finds you all in one piece.

Until the next sitting of the council,
Thomas Boleyn, Earl of Wiltshire

